==Trivia==
*Morningstar Isle's Japanese name, Myōjō-oki no Shima (明星おきの島, "Morningstar Island"), is a reference to [[wikipedia:Oki Islands|Oki no Shima]] (隠岐の島), a cluster of islands in Shimane Prefecture, Japan. These islands have been inhabited since the Japanese Paleolithic era, connecting them to [[Uncanny Legends]]' theme of an ancient past.
*Some of the stages' names appear to reference mythology:
**[[Icarus' Instinct]] refers to the Greek legend of Daedalus' son [[wikipedia:Icarus|Icarus]]. In the legend, he ignored his father's warnings to not fly too close to the sun, melting his wax wings and sending him to a watery grave in the Icarian Sea.
**[[Rainbow Bridge Toll]] may refer to [[wikipedia:Bifröst|Bifröst]], a burning rainbow bridge in Norse mythology that connects the realm of mortals, Midgard (Earth), with the realm of the gods, Asgard.
**Since its Japanese name translates to "Cats-turned-constellations", [[Cats in the Stars]] may be a reference to myths of people and animals turning into or being memorialized as constellations. This trope is most prevalent in Greek mythology as [[wiktionary:catasterism|catasterism]]; for example, [[wikipedia:Leo (constellation)|Leo]] is said to be the [[wikipedia:Nemean Lion|Nemean Lion]], placed in the sky by Zeus after Heracles defeated it.

